UPDATE companies SET description='Southwest Wire Rope Inc was founded in 1966 in New Iberia, Louisiana, to address demand for reliable wire rope and rigging products from industries along the Gulf Coast. The company began as a supplier of wire rope and related hardware, expanding its product line over the decades to serve diversified markets worldwide.

The company operates three full-service locations in Texas and Louisiana, stocking a complete range of lifting products including wire rope slings, nylon slings, round slings, chain, shackles, thimbles, sockets, and other hardware. Beyond distribution, Southwest Wire Rope provides engineering services such as engineered lifting device design, lift planning, and load testing up to 1.5 million pounds. Its fabrication shop produces below-the-hook lifting devices—spreader bars, spreader beams, lifting beams, lifting frames, padeyes, reel lifters, and custom assemblies—designed to ASME B30.20 and BTH-1 standards. Additional services include field spooling of wire and synthetic rope (under the Haynes Wire Rope trade name), on-site rigging gear inspections using Tessalink software, and lifting gear rentals.

The company differentiates itself through its ISO 9001:2015 quality management system certified by DNV, the proprietary Gold Strand wire rope trademark introduced in 1983, and in-house testing capabilities calibrated to ASTM E4. Engineering expertise is backed by professional engineers who perform structural calculations using Mathcad, SolidWorks, and ANSYS finite element analysis, validated by proof load testing.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire rope sling fabrication", "Nylon sling fabrication", "Round sling fabrication", "Chain sling fabrication", "Shackle, thimble, socket, and hardware supply", "Engineered lifting device design", "Lift planning and rigging diagrams", "Proof load testing (up to 1.5 million lbs)", "Destructive break testing", "Field wire rope spooling", "Field synthetic rope spooling", "On-site rigging gear inspection", "Lifting gear rental", "Steel fabrication", "Below-the-hook lifting device fabrication (spreader bars, spreader beams, lifting beams, lifting frames, padeyes, reel lifters, cylinder lifters, forklift adapters, material baskets, skip pans, lifting tongs, rigging racks)", "Structural calculation (Mathcad)", "3D modeling and 2D drawing (SolidWorks)", "Finite element analysis (ANSYS Workbench)", "Load cell distribution (Crosby Straightpoint authorized distributor)"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Wire rope", "Nylon", "Synthetic rope", "Chain", "Steel"], "equipment": ["Computerized test beds calibrated to ASTM E4", "Tessalink asset management software", "Mathcad", "SolidWorks", "ANSYS Workbench"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 quality management system certified by DNV", "Gold Strand wire rope trademark since 1983", "Proof load and destructive testing capacity up to 1.5 million lbs", "Engineered lifting devices designed to ASME B30.20 and BTH-1", "On-site spooling and inspection services under Haynes Wire Rope name"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1966 in New Iberia, Louisiana -> db", "Three full-service locations in Texas & Louisiana -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certified by DNV -> /about", "Gold Strand wire rope trademark introduced 1983 -> /about", "Testing capabilities up to 1.5 million lbs -> /about", "Authorized distributor of Crosby Straightpoint products -> /", "Engineering services: engineered lifting devices, lift plans, load testing -> /", "Fabrication of below-the-hook lifting devices per ASME B30.20 and BTH-1 -> /services", "Field spooling under Haynes Wire Rope trade name -> /services", "On-site rigging gear inspection with Tessalink software -> /services", "Lifting gear rental (skip pans, spreader beams) -> /services", "Proof load and destructive testing calibrated to ASTM E4 -> /services", "Structural calculations using Mathcad, SolidWorks, ANSYS Workbench -> /services", "Lift plans for complex lifts -> /services"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, we are a prime supplier of material handling, lifting & mooring products globally. Authorized distributor of Crosby Straightpoint products.", "founded_year": "1966", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='southwest-wire-rope-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Spartronics operates a 100,000-square-foot electromechanical manufacturing facility in Watertown, South Dakota. The company provides contract manufacturing services for complex electronic and electromechanical products across regulated industries.

The facility specializes in printed circuit board assembly (PCBA) using surface-mount, through-hole, and flex-circuit technologies, along with electromechanical sub-assembly and full box-build integration. Capabilities include automated optical inspection, X-ray inspection, flying-probe and in-circuit testing, environmental stress screening, conformal coating, and functional test development. The site supports new product introduction (NPI), prototyping, and volume production, backed by supply chain management and aftermarket services such as repair, refurbishment, and obsolescence management.

Spartronics serves medical device, life sciences, instrumentation and control, commercial aerospace, defense, and space sectors. Customers include original equipment manufacturers requiring FDA-registered, ISO 13485-certified production for devices such as cardiovascular monitors, neuroablation systems, patient-warming equipment, and RF audio transmission modules. The company also supports aerospace and defense programs requiring AS9100 and ITAR compliance.

The company emphasizes a holistic product ownership mentality, combining in-house PCBA and top-level assembly under one roof. Its quality system adheres to standards including ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, AS9100, IEC 60601-1, and IPC-A-610 Class III, with dedicated project managers and cross-functional teams for each program.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100','ISO 13485:2016','ISO 14001','NADCAP','ITAR','21 CFR 820','21 CFR Part 11','FDA cGMP/QSR Registered','IEC 60601-1','IECEX','IPC-A-610 Class I, II, III','IPC-7711/7721','ISO 14971:2007','RoHS','REACH']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Printed Circuit Board Assembly (PCBA)", "Surface Mount Technology (SMT) Assembly", "Through-Hole Assembly", "Flex Circuit Assembly", "Mixed Technology Circuit Card Assembly", "Electromechanical Sub-Assembly", "Full Box-Build Integration", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "X-Ray Inspection", "Flying Probe Testing", "In-Circuit Testing (ICT)", "Boundary Scan Testing", "Functional Test Development & Fixturing", "Environmental Stress Screening (ESS)", "Conformal Coating", "High-Pot Testing", "New Product Introduction (NPI) Support", "Prototyping", "Supply Chain Management", "KanBan Inventory Management", "Lean Cellular Manufacturing", "Design for Excellence (DFX)", "Sustaining Engineering", "Aftermarket Repair & Refurbishment"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Life Sciences", "Instrumentation & Control", "Commercial Aerospace", "Defense", "Space"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100,000 sq. ft. electromechanical footprint with state-of-the-art SMT placement capabilities", "In-house PCBA and top-level assembly creating holistic product ownership", "FDA-registered and ISO 13485:2016 certified for medical device manufacturing", "AS9100 and ITAR registered for aerospace and defense programs", "Full product lifecycle support from NPI through aftermarket services"], "facts_used": ["Location: Watertown, South Dakota -> /", "Facility size: 100,000 sq. ft. -> /", "Vertical markets: Medical Devices, Life Sciences, Instrumentation & Control, Commercial Aerospace -> /", "Key capabilities list (AOI, PCBA, conformal coating, etc.) -> /", "Certifications & standards list (ISO 9001:2015, AS9100, ISO 13485:2016, etc.) -> /", "Application experience examples (cardiovascular, neuroablation, patient warming, RF audio) -> /", "Technological expertise (accelerometer, catheter monitoring, RF ablation) -> /", "Contract manufacturing services description (PCBA, subsystem integration, full-box build) -> /about", "Global factory network (US and Vietnam) -> /about", "Service offerings (value-added engineering, manufacturing readiness, supply chain, quality, logistics, aftermarket) -> /services", "Quality system details (MRR, PRR, APQP, DHR, DMR, 3D automated verification) -> /quality", "Industries served per quality page (commercial aerospace, defense, space, life sciences, medical devices, instrumentation and control) -> /quality"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our manufacturing services are comprehensive, ranging from printed circuit board assembly (PCBA) and subsystem integration to full-box build (high-level assemblies).", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered", "Export compliance support"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='spartronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1942 as a division of Lewis Engineering Company in Naugatuck, Connecticut, Specialty Cable Corporation (SCC) began producing highly engineered wire and cable for military and aerospace applications. The company now operates a 65,000‑square‑foot facility in Wallingford, Connecticut.

SCC engineers and manufactures a range of wire and cable products, including Mil‑spec aerospace cables for engine and airframe systems, audio interconnect cables optimized for distortion‑free transmission, and cables used in medical heart monitors and fetal monitoring equipment. The company has developed proprietary manufacturing methods such as a printing technique that ensures repeatable quality, and it produces cables rated for temperatures from –150 °C to over 1,400 °C, with resistance to chemicals and precise dimensional control.

The company serves aerospace, defense, medical, audio, and industrial markets. Its products are found in aircraft engine control systems, fetal heart monitors, and other demanding applications requiring high reliability in hostile environments.

SCC emphasizes a value‑engineered philosophy, aiming to provide the right solution at a sensible price even for small quantities. Its quality system is certified to AS9100D and ISO 9001:2015, and the company highlights its ability to apply technologies across markets to solve custom cable challenges.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100D','ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire and cable engineering", "Custom cable manufacturing", "Proprietary printing technique", "Mil-spec aerospace cable production (M27500 per NEMA WC27500-2015)", "Audio interconnect cable production", "Medical cable manufacturing (heart monitors, fetal monitors)", "High-temperature cable manufacturing (\u2013150\u202f\u00b0C to 1,400\u202f\u00b0C)", "Chemical-resistant cable manufacturing", "Electrical, materials, and process engineering", "Quality assurance: visual and dimensional compliance verification", "Certified test reports and certificates of conformance", "Value-engineered design for small quantities"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense/Military", "Medical", "Audio", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary printing technique for repeatable high\u2011quality results", "Custom cables rated from \u2013150\u202f\u00b0C to over 1,400\u202f\u00b0C", "AS9100D and ISO\u202f9001:2015 certified quality system", "Value\u2011engineered approach for cost\u2011effective solutions even in small quantities", "65,000\u2011sq\u2011ft manufacturing facility in Wallingford, CT"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1942 as a division of Lewis Engineering Company -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Wallingford, Connecticut -> /capabilities", "65,000 sq ft facility -> /capabilities", "AS9100D and ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /, /about-us, /capabilities", "CAGE Code 60685 -> /, /about-us, /capabilities", "Produces Mil-spec aerospace cables for engine and airframe -> /", "Audio interconnect cables for distortion-free transmissi