UPDATE companies SET description='Spike Electric Controls was founded in 1965 in Houston, Texas, as an American electrical equipment manufacturer. The company designs and builds power distribution and control systems for critical infrastructure.

The company engineers and manufactures low- and medium-voltage switchgear, gas-insulated switchgear, and custom power distribution systems. Its vertically integrated operations span electrical engineering, precision machining, forming, welding, finishing, assembly, and in-house testing, supported by a workforce of 500 to 999 employees.

Spike serves commercial, industrial, and utility sectors, with notable projects including power infrastructure for Google data centers, hazardous-location switchracks for Marathon Petroleum, fast-track automatic transfer switch systems for Milton Caterpillar, and custom breaker cells for the Downtown Houston Tunnel installation.

Founded on a stewardship philosophy, Spike emphasizes accountability by keeping engineering, manufacturing, quality assurance, and post-delivery support under one roof, aiming to reduce handoffs and accelerate delivery for mission-critical applications.', certifications=ARRAY['UL 1558']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical engineering and system integration", "Precision machining and forming", "Welding", "Finishing", "Final assembly", "In-house testing and quality assurance", "Post-installation service and support", "Switchgear retrofits", "Hazardous-location equipment design", "Packaged power solutions"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Industrial", "Power Utilities", "Data Centers", "Oil & Gas", "Infrastructure Construction"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated engineering, manufacturing, testing, and support in-house", "Fast turnaround times on custom power systems", "Custom engineering for complex specifications", "24/7 post-delivery support", "In-house control over quality and project schedules"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1965 -> db", "Headquarters Houston, Texas -> db", "Employee count 500-999 -> db", "Certification UL 1558 -> db", "Products: low/medium voltage switchgear, gas-insulated switchgear, custom power distribution -> /", "Industries served: commercial, industrial, power utilities -> db", "Capabilities: engineering, manufacturing, testing, service -> /capabilities", "Projects: Google data center, Marathon Petroleum, Milton Caterpillar, Downtown Houston Tunnel -> /", "Vertically integrated in-house operations -> /about", "Stewardship founding philosophy -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Spike engineers and manufactures low- and medium-voltage switchgear, gas-insulated switchgear, and custom power distribution systems", "founded_year": "1965", "employee_count": "500-999", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "exp