UPDATE companies SET description='Spinnaker Contract Manufacturing, Inc. was founded in 1976 in Tilton, New Hampshire, and has remained family-owned since its inception. The company began as a New England-based electronics contract manufacturer focused on providing turnkey assembly services to regional OEMs.

Operating from a 30,000-square-foot facility that includes a dedicated 15,000-square-foot electro-mechanical assembly area, Spinnaker runs four high-speed SMT lines capable of placing 01005 components, through-hole PCB assembly, custom wire harness fabrication using Schleuniger automated equipment, and full box-build integration. The workforce of 51–200 employees supports turnkey supply chain management, new product introduction, and direct fulfillment.

The company serves medical device, defense, telecommunications, industrial automation, semiconductor capital equipment, and commercial electronics OEMs. Its customer base includes organizations whose products are too complex for smaller contract manufacturers but whose volumes do not attract large-scale EMS providers, as well as those requiring close collaboration during early design phases.

Spinnaker emphasizes flexibility in staffing and equipment allocation per project, rigorous test and inspection processes including flying probe and 3D X-ray, and a customer-centric philosophy aimed at exceeding expectations through responsiveness, on-time delivery, and quality discipline.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015 Certified','ISO 13485:2016 Certified (Medical Devices)','ITAR Registered','IPC-A-610 Class 2 & Class 3 Certified','IPC/WHMA-A-620 Cable & Wire Harness Certified','UL / CSA Approved Facility','RoHS & Lead-Free Compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Printed Circuit Board Assembly (PCBA - SMT & Through-Hole)", "High-Speed Surface Mount Technology (4 SMT Lines down to 01005)", "Custom Cable & Wire Harness Assembly (Schleuniger automated crimp/strip)", "Electro-Mechanical Assembly & Full Box-Build Integration", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI) & In-Line Solder Paste Inspection (SPI)", "2D & 3D X-Ray Inspection (Dage Quadra 3)", "Flying Probe Testing (SPEA 4060S2) & Functional Testing", "Cable & Harness Continuity / Hi-Pot Testing (Cirris systems)", "Conformal Coating, Potting & Enclosure Assembly", "Turnkey Supply Chain Management, NPI & Direct Fulfillment", "Laser Engraving, Precision Marking & Enclosure Customization"], "industries": ["Medical Devices & Healthcare Technology", "Defense & Homeland Security", "Telecommunications & Networking", "Industrial Automation, Robotics & Controls", "Semiconductor & Capital Equipment", "Commercial Electronics & Renewable Energy", "Instrumentation"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Schleuniger automated crimp/strip machines", "SPEA 4060S2 flying probe tester", "Dage Quadra 3 3D X-ray inspection system", "Cirris cable/harness test systems", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI) system", "In-line Solder Paste Inspection (SPI) system", "Four high-speed SMT placement lines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned since 1976", "30,000 sq ft facility with 15,000 sq ft electro-mechanical assembly area", "Four high-speed SMT lines capable of 01005 placement", "ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 13485:2016 certified, ITAR registered", "In-house flying probe (SPEA) and 3D X-ray (Dage Quadra 3) inspection"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1976 -> db, /", "Family-owned since 1976 -> /", "Headquarters Tilton, New Hampshire -> db, /", "30,000 sq ft facility with 15,000 sq ft electro-mechanical area -> db", "Employee count 51-200 -> db", "Four high-speed SMT lines down to 01005 -> db, /services", "Schleuniger automated crimp/strip for wire harnesses -> db", "SPEA 4060S2 flying probe tester -> db", "Dage Quadra 3 3D X-ray inspection -> db", "Cirris cable/harness test systems -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> db", "ISO 13485:2016 certified -> db", "ITAR registered -> db", "IPC-A-610 Class 2 & 3 certified -> db", "IPC/WHMA-A-620 certified -> db", "UL/CSA approved facility -> db", "RoHS & Lead-Free compliant -> db", "Industries: Medical, Defense, Telecom, Industrial, Semiconductor, Commercial -> db, /", "Customer type: complex products, mid-volume, early collaboration -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our core competency is electronics contract manufacturing", "founded_year": "1976", "employee_count": "51-200", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='spinnaker-contract-manufacturing-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Spring Solar was founded in 2016 in Bluffdale, Utah, as a family-owned business focused on residential and commercial solar installation. The company began with a mission to make solar power accessible and affordable for homeowners and businesses across the Intermountain West.

The company designs, permits, and installs custom solar photovoltaic systems, including rooftop panels, inverters, and battery storage. Its team manages the entire process from initial energy assessment through final inspection and system activation, and provides real-time production monitoring for every installation. Spring Solar serves customers throughout Utah, Wyoming, and Colorado, with a service area that includes Salt Lake City, Park City, and surrounding communities.

Spring Solar works primarily with homeowners whose monthly electricity bills exceed $100 and with businesses seeking a return on investment within five years. The company has installed systems for residents in Bluffdale, West Jordan, and Draper, as well as for commercial clients looking to reduce operating costs and capture tax incentives.

Spring Solar differentiates itself with a low-price guarantee that matches or beats any competitor’s quote, 25-year product and manufacturer warranties, and a family-owned structure that emphasizes personalized service. The firm is also a Triple‑E Installer Partner with APsystems, offering microinverter technology backed by a 2026 Best of SLC Award.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar system design and engineering", "Permitting and inspection management", "Residential solar panel installation", "Commercial solar panel installation", "Inverter installation and configuration", "Battery storage system installation", "Real-time system monitoring", "Energy consumption assessment"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["APsystems microinverters"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Low-price guarantee: match or beat any competitor\u2019s quote", "Family-owned with personalized customer service", "25-year product and manufacturer warranties", "Real-time production monitoring on every system", "Triple\u2011E Installer Partner with APsystems microinverters"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2016 -> db", "Family-owned -> /", "Headquarters Bluffdale, Utah -> db and /", "Serves Utah, Wyoming, Colorado -> /", "Low-price guarantee -> /", "25-year product and manufacturer warranties -> /", "Real-time production monitoring -> /", "Triple-E Installer Partner with APsystems -> /", "2026 Best of SLC Award -> /", "Residential and commercial installation -> /", "Design, permits, installation, activation -> /", "Battery storage and inverters -> /", "Energy assessment -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Our experienced team handles every step\u2014from design and permits to final inspection and activation", "founded_year": "2016", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='spring-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='St. Johns Packaging was founded in 1954 by René J. Leclair in Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu, Quebec, when the banker and consultant acquired a small waxed-paper operation on the verge of bankruptcy. The business began with fewer than ten employees in a 5,000-square-foot plant serving local bakeries and meat packers. Ownership remains with the Leclair family, now in its third generation, and the company is headquartered in Greensboro, North Carolina.

Today the firm operates as a vertically integrated manufacturer of flexible packaging, producing blown polyethylene film (up to five layers), flexographic printing up to ten colors, wicket bags, laminated pouches, lidding films, and laser-perforated fresh-produce films. Eleven facilities across Canada, the United States, Mexico, the United Kingdom, China, Vietnam, and Australia employ more than 950 people and provide capabilities from extrusion through finished bags.

The company supplies food and consumer-product brands in bakery (bread and bun bags), personal care (feminine hygiene and incontinence packaging), pet food, frozen foods, dairy, and fresh produce. Recent acquisitions such as Amcor''s UK bakery business and Australia''s Flexible Packaging Solutions have expanded its reach in European and Asia-Pacific markets.

St. Johns emphasizes reliability, flexibility, and responsiveness, focusing on a limited customer base to deliver optimal value. Sustainability is a stated priority: all polyethylene wicket bags are recyclable, and the company aims to reduce both plastic and food waste through economically viable packaging solutions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Blown film extrusion (up to 5-layer)", "Flexographic printing up to 10 colors", "Wicket bag manufacturing", "Solvent-less lamination", "Bag making (various styles)", "Laminated pouch manufacturing", "Printed rewind", "Laser perforation", "Lidding film production", "Stand-up pouch manufacturing", "Flat pouch manufacturing", "Box bag manufacturing", "Fresh produce film converting", "Graphic services"], "industries": ["Bakery", "Personal Care", "Pet Food", "Food Products", "Frozen Foods", "Fresh Produce", "Dairy", "Healthcare"], "materials": ["Polyethylene (PE)", "Polypropylene", "Cellophane"], "equipment": ["5-layer blown film extrusion lines", "10-color flexographic presses", "Wicket bag machines", "Laser perforation equipment", "Solvent-less lamination equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Reliability, flexibility, and responsiveness", "Focus on delivering optimal value to a limited number of customers", "Vertically integrated from blown film extrusion to finished bags", "100% of PE wicket bags recyclable", "State-of-the-art 5-layer blown film extrusion lines"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1954 by Ren\u00e9 J. Leclair -> /about-us", "Family-owned, Leclair family control -> /about-us", "Headquarters Greensboro, NC -> db", "Vertically integrated manufacturer of flexible packaging -> /about-us", "11 facilities across 7 countries -> /", "More than 950 employees -> /", "Processes: blown film extrusion up to 5-layer, flexographic printing up to 10 colors, wicket bags, solvent-less lamination, pouches, laser perforation, lidding films -> /, /about-us", "Markets: Bakery, Personal Care, Pet Food, Food Products, Frozen Foods, Fresh Produce, Dairy -> /, /about-us", "Differentiators: reliability, flexibility, responsiveness; focus on limited customer base -> /about-us", "Sustainability: 100% PE wicket bags recyclable -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "vertically integrated manufacturer of flexible packaging products that are sold to leading food and consumer product companies", "founded_year": "1954", "employee_count": "950+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='st-johns-packaging' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Stammy''s Steel was founded in 2012 in Oakdale, Connecticut by a welder and engineer whose background in nuclear engineering and passion for motorsports led to a fabrication business. The owner began by building custom off-road parts for a trophy truck project and later expanded into the local drifting scene.

The shop provides welding, repairs, and fabrication services, including precision cutting, roll cage fabrication, and metal bending. All bending and welding are performed in-house to control quality and cost. The company also offers mobile welding and repair services across the greater New England region, equipped for plasma cutting and gouging.

Stammy''s Steel serves motorsports enthusiasts, off-road vehicle builders, automotive clients, and industrial equipment operators. Customers range from drift teams needing roll cages to facilities requiring large equipment repairs and one-off custom projects.

