UPDATE companies SET description='Standard Spring Parts operates from Arden Hills, Minnesota, tracing its roots to 1923 when Percy Emory incorporated Standard Spring Co. in St. Paul. The company began as a blacksmith shop forging leaf springs with fire, hammers, and anvils. In 1944, blacksmith Hilding Ostrom purchased the business, establishing a family lineage that continues today under third‑generation owner Scott Ostrom, his wife Joy, and their son Garrett.

The firm no longer manufactures springs; since 2010 it has functioned as a distributor and warehouse for new leaf‑spring assemblies and related suspension hardware. Its catalog covers custom‑bent U‑bolts, trunnion stands, spring pins, insulator pads, and bolster springs for brands such as Mack, Freightliner, Peterbilt, Hendrickson, and Fruehauf.

The product range addresses front and rear suspensions for Mack Camelback, Freightliner TufTrac, Peterbilt Low Mount Air Leaf, and Hendrickson Haulmaax systems, among others.

