UPDATE companies SET description='Stark Electronics Inc. was founded in 1938 in New Brighton, Minnesota, as a regional distributor of electronic components. The company serves OEMs ranging from startups to Fortune 500 firms with a line card that includes brands such as Alpha Wire, Conxall, and Orion Fans. In 2024, Marsh Electronics acquired Stark to expand its product portfolio and strengthen its presence in the industrial electronics market, providing Stark with enhanced distribution capabilities and access to a broader customer base.

Through its subsidiary Absolute Quality Manufacturing (AQM), Stark offers custom electrical solutions. AQM produces custom wire harnesses up to 100 feet in length with connectors from Deutsch, Amphenol, and MIL‑STD, as well as cable assemblies ranging from 30 AWG to 4/0 and multi‑conductor cables. The shop also builds terminal block and DIN rail assemblies using franchised lines like Dinkle, UL 508A certified electrical control panels, electro‑mechanical assemblies, and turn‑key panel and box builds.

The combined organization serves the automotive, agriculture, and transportation industries, among others. Its customer base includes OEMs in sectors that require ruggedized cable assemblies for fertilizer sensors, transportation systems, and agricultural equipment.

Stark emphasizes a commitment to quality and customer satisfaction built on decades of experience. The company states that it continuously invests in staff training and cutting‑edge technology to remain at the forefront of the industry, and that its in‑house function testing ensures each assembly meets exacting demands.', certifications=ARRAY['UL 508A']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom wire harnesses", "Custom cable assemblies", "Terminal block & DIN rail assemblies", "Electrical control panels (UL 508A certified)", "Electro-mechanical assemblies", "Turn-key panel & box builds"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Agriculture", "Transportation"], "materials": ["Wire (30 AWG to 4/0)", "Multi-conductor cables", "Connectors (Deutsch, Amphenol, MIL-STD)", "Terminal blocks (Dinkle)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["UL 508A certified panel shop", "Custom wire harnesses up to 100 feet with Deutsch, Amphenol, MIL\u2011STD connectors", "Cable assemblies from 30 AWG to 4/0 and multi\u2011conductor cables", "Terminal block & DIN rail assemblies using franchised lines (Dinkle)", "In\u2011house function testing for electro\u2011mechanical assemblies"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1938 -> db", "Headquarters New Brighton, Minnesota -> db", "Acquired by Marsh Electronics in 2024 -> /", "Distributor with line card including Alpha Wire, Conxall, Orion Fans -> /", "Parent company of Absolute Quality Manufacturing (AQM) -> /", "Custom wire harnesses up to 100 feet with Deutsch, Amphenol, MIL-STD connectors -> /capabilities", "Cable assemblies from 30 AWG to 4/0 and multi-conductor cables -> /capabilities", "Terminal block & DIN rail assemblies using franchised lines like Dinkle -> /capabilities", "UL 508A certified electrical control panels -> /capabilities", "Electro-mechanical assemblies with in-house function testing -> /capabilities", "Turn-key panel & box builds -> /capabilities", "Industries served: automotive, agriculture, transportation -> db, /capabilities", "Certification: UL 508A -> /capabilities", "Materials: wire, cables, connectors, terminal blocks -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Welcome to Stark Electronics, your trusted regional distributor supporting OEMs worldwide since 1938.", "founded_year": "1938", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='stark-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Steel Fabricators LLC was founded in 1962 in Oakland Park, Florida. The company operates its main offices in Fort Lauderdale and maintains a regional office in Orlando. It functions as a subsidiary of FabSouth, a larger construction group.

The firm specializes in structural steel fabrication and erection, offering complete in-house capabilities that cover the full project lifecycle. It holds AISC certification as both a fabricator and erector, and is a Florida-licensed general contractor. The company reports a bonding capacity of $125 million per project and $625 million in aggregate, with an experience modification rate (EMR) of 0.67. Its portfolio includes hundreds of projects nationwide, ranging from commercial buildings to large-scale entertainment venues.

Steel Fabricators serves clients in commercial construction, entertainment, marine infrastructure, and public-sector projects. Notable projects include the F3 Marina in Fort Lauderdale, the Broward County Convention Center, the Formula One facilities at Hard Rock Stadium in Miami Gardens, Star Wars: Galaxy''s Edge in Orlando, Hard Rock Live in Hollywood, and Port of Miami Cruise Terminal A.

The company distinguishes itself through its integrated in-house fabrication and erection teams, which it says enable fast response, maximum flexibility, and coordinated execution across all project phases. It positions itself as a single-source structural steel partner capable of handling projects regardless of schedule, scope, size, or complexity.', certifications=ARRAY['AISC Certified Fabricator & Erector','Florida Licensed General Contractor']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "Steel erection", "General contracting"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Entertainment and theme parks", "Sports stadiums", "Marine and port facilities", "Convention centers", "Public sector"], "materials": ["Structural steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house steel erection and fabrication under one roof", "AISC certified fabricator and erector", "Florida licensed general contractor", "Bonding capacity of $125M single / $625M aggregate", "EMR of 0.67"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1962 -> db", "Headquarters in Oakland Park, Florida -> db", "Main offices in Fort Lauderdale, FL -> /", "Regional office in Orlando, FL -> /", "Subsidiary of FabSouth -> /", "Structural steel fabrication and erection -> /", "AISC certified fabricator and erector -> /", "Florida licensed general contractor -> /", "Bond capacity $125M single, $625M aggregate -> /", "EMR 0.67 -> /", "Projects: F3 Marina, Broward County Convention Center, Formula One at Hard Rock Stadium, Star Wars: Galaxy''s Edge, Hard Rock Live, Port of Miami Cruise Terminal A -> /", "Single-source structural steel fabrication company -> /", "In-house capabilities for fast response and coordination -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are the single-source structural steel fabrication company of choice", "founded_year": "1962", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='steel-fabricators-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Steel Plate Fabricators, headquartered in Knoxville, Tennessee, traces its roots to 1921 when A.J. Russell and his son founded A.J. Russell & Son in a home outbuilding in the Lonsdale community. The business incorporated as Knoxville Sheet Metal Works in the 1940s under Calvin and Helen Russell, then shifted to heavier plate fabrication in 1964 under David and Merle Russell, adopting the Steel Plate Fabricators name. In 2007, fourth-generation owners Mike and Anna Russell purchased the company, continuing the family-owned operation.

The company operates a 140,000-square-foot facility on 10 acres equipped with twelve overhead cranes (up to 30-ton capacity) and a range of CNC cutting, forming, machining, and welding equipment. Its 55 full-time employees provide custom fabrication, structural steel, CNC laser, plasma, and waterjet cutting, press braking, rolling, sawing, robotic and manual welding, blasting, painting, powder coating, and assembly. The shop handles one-off prototypes through large-scale production runs, including nuclear waste containers, beam weldments, tank fabrication, and turnkey assemblies.

Steel Plate Fabricators serves energy and utility companies, biomedical device manufacturers, agricultural equipment builders, transportation (automotive, rail, marine), heavy industry (mining, oil and gas), food and beverage producers, commercial and residential construction, and government agencies. The firm also supports technology and general manufacturing sectors with reverse engineering and on-site repair services.

