UPDATE companies SET description='Steel Specialties, LLC was established in 2006 by Greg Pendergrass and Randy Cunningham in Dunbar, West Virginia. The privately held company later added Brian Cunningham as Operations Manager, bringing together a team with over 100 years of combined steel fabrication experience. In 2016, the firm acquired a 33,000-square-foot facility in Point Pleasant, WV, which now serves as its headquarters alongside the original Dunbar operations.

The company operates a total of 47,700 square feet under roof dedicated to steel fabrication. Its services span structural steel fabrication (columns, beams, trusses, tube frames, floor grating, checkered plate, anchor bolts), custom handrail, ladder, and walkway systems (pipe handrail, bar and rod handrail, caged ladders, platforms), specialty equipment fabrication (belt conveyors, screw conveyors, sampling systems, processing equipment, feeders), and chutework fabrication in mild steel, stainless steel, AR-lined, and ceramic-lined configurations. In-house capabilities also include blasting and painting (with a roto blast machine), engineering detailing in 2D AutoCAD or 3D SolidWorks, and galvanizing coordinated through regional hot-dip facilities.

Steel Specialties serves commercial and industrial clients across the Tri-State Area and globally. The company emphasizes repeat customer satisfaction driven by demanding schedules and quality requirements.

The firm’s stated mission is to provide fabricated products that meet or exceed client requirements by following industry standards such as ISO, ASTM, and AISC. It differentiates itself by offering a “one-stop shop” through integrated detailing, fabrication, blasting, painting, and galvanizing services, allowing clients to consolidate subcontracts.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural Steel Fabrication", "Custom Handrail, Ladder, & Walkway Fabrication", "Specialty Equipment Fabrication", "Chutework Fabrication (Mild Steel, Stainless Steel, AR Lined, Ceramic Lined)", "Blasting and Painting", "Engineering Detailing (2D AutoCAD, 3D SolidWorks)", "Galvanizing Coordination"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Mild Steel", "Stainless Steel", "AR Plate", "Ceramic Lined Steel"], "equipment": ["Roto blast machine"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full-service fabrication shop with in-house detailing, blasting, painting, and galvanizing coordination", "Engineering detailing offered in 2D AutoCAD or 3D SolidWorks", "Galvanizing managed through regional hot-dip facilities to eliminate separate subcontracts", "Blasting performed via hand-held techniques or roto blast machine", "Repeat customer satisfaction driving success since 2006"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2006 by Greg Pendergrass and Randy Cunningham -> /about", "Privately held company -> /about", "Brian Cunningham joined as Operations Manager -> /about", "Facility growth: 7,500 sq ft in Dunbar (2006), added 7,200 sq ft (2010), acquired 33,000 sq ft in Point Pleasant (2016), total 47,700 sq ft -> /about", "Services: structural steel fabrication, custom handrail/ladder/walkway, specialty equipment fabrication, chutework fabrication, blasting/painting, engineering detailing, galvanizing -> /services", "Blasting performed by hand held or roto blast machine -> /services", "Engineering detailing in 2D AutoCAD or 3D SolidWorks -> /servi