UPDATE companies SET description='Sumiden Wire Products Corporation was founded in 1979 in Stockton, California, as the first U.S. production facility established by Japan’s Sumitomo Electric Industries (SEI). The company operates as a wholly-owned subsidiary of SEI and is headquartered in Dickson, Tennessee.

The company manufactures seven-wire prestressed concrete steel strand (PC strand) to ASTM A416 specifications in uncoated, epoxy-coated, and stainless steel grades, as well as stainless spring wire, stainless medical wire, nickel-plated carbon steel wire, and industrial alloy products. Production spans three plants in California, Tennessee, and Texas, with capabilities including wire drawing, nickel electroplating to custom thicknesses, epoxy coating, and dedicated inventory programs for medical customers. Environmental Product Declarations are available for each PC strand variant.

Sumiden Wire serves the construction industry — supplying strand for bridges, buildings, parking structures, and home foundations — along with aerospace, automotive, consumer, military, and medical device manufacturers. Medical applications include orthodontic wire, guidewires, orthopaedic components, and endoscopy devices. The company also supports durable goods producers.

Sumiden Wire states its mission is to “help Build America” by providing superior-quality steel strand for concrete structures nationwide. Differentiators cited include its global supplier network, seasoned local management, customer service, and innovations such as stainless steel and epoxy-coated PC strand plus ultra-fine wire for surgical catheters. As part of the Sumitomo Electric Group, the company adheres to the group’s Code of Conduct.', certifications=ARRAY['ASTM A416']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PC strand manufacturing (uncoated, epoxy-coated, stainless steel)", "Stainless spring wire production", "Stainless medical wire production", "Nickel electroplating on carbon steel wire", "Epoxy coating", "Custom thickness and ductility specification", "Bright finish processing", "Concentricity control", "Adhesion testing", "Customer dedicated inventory programs", "Environmental Product Declaration documentation", "Pre-tension and post-tension strand production", "Stay cable production", "Wire drawing"], "industries": ["Construction", "Aerospace", "Automotive", "Consumer", "Military", "Medical devices", "Durable goods"], "materials": ["Carbon steel wire", "Stainless steel", "Nickel", "Epoxy coating"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First U.S. production facility established by Sumitomo Electric Industries (1979)", "Largest producer of stainless steel spring wire in the U.S. since 2016 acquisition", "Three manufacturing plants enabling nationwide supply (California, Tennessee, Texas)", "Environmental Product Declarations for uncoated, epoxy-coated, and stainless steel PC strand", "Ultra-smooth surface, bright finish, and customer-dedicated inventory programs for medical wire"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 in Stockton, California -> /about", "Wholly-owned subsidiary of Sumitomo Electric Industries -> /about, products list", "Headquarters in Dickson, Tennessee -> db, /about", "Second plant opened in Dickson 1989 -> /about", "Third PC strand plant in Dayton, Texas 2017 -> /about", "Largest producer of stainless steel spring wire in US since 2016 -> /about", "Manufactures PC strand per ASTM A416 -> /, /about", "Products: PC strand (uncoated, epoxy-coated, stainless), stainless spring wire, stainless medical wire, nickel plated wire, industrial alloys -> /, /about", "Three manufacturing plants: California, Tennessee, Texas -> /, /about", "Capabilities: nickel electroplating, epoxy coating, custom thickness/ductility, bright finish, concentricity, adhesion, dedicated inventory programs -> /, /about", "Environmental Product Declarations for PC strand variants -> /", "Industries: construction (bridges, buildings, parking, foundations), aerospace, automotive, consumer, military, medical (orthodontic, guidewire, orthopaedic, endoscopy), durable goods -> /, /about", "Mission: help Build America, superior quality, nationwide delivery -> /about", "Global network, seasoned management, superior service -> /about", "Innovations: stainless steel PC strand, epoxy-coated PC strand, ultra-fine wire for surgical catheters -> /about", "Part of Sumitomo Electric Group, adheres to Code of Conduct -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Sumiden Wire produces and supplies high-quality prestressed concrete strand from our manufacturing plants in California, Tennessee and Texas.", "founded_year": "1979", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sumiden-wire-products-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company operates its North American headquarters from Farmington Hills, Michigan, and maintains additional locations across the continent under the leadership of President Kazuyoshi Nakai.

SEWS designs, develops, and manufactures wiring harnesses, electronic components, electric wire, and electrified-vehicle-related products for the automotive sector. Its portfolio spans complete harness assemblies, integrated electronics, and advanced product development services aimed at systems integration and modularization. The company emphasizes advanced manufacturing technology and global technical development across its North American footprint.

The company serves automotive original equipment manufacturers and tier suppliers, providing electrical distribution systems that address safety, comfort, fuel economy, and connectivity requirements. Its products are engineered for the evolving “automotive society” that connects vehicles, people, and infrastructure.

SEWS states its mission is to be the global leader delivering innovative electrical distribution systems that meet the demands of the ever-changing automotive market. The Sumitomo Spirit and core values—emphasizing efficiency, reliability, cost-effectiveness, and developing people to improve manufacturing—underpin its differentiation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wiring harness design and manufacturing", "Electronic component design and manufacturing", "Electric wire production", "Electrified vehicle product development", "Advanced product development", "Systems integration", "Modularization", "Global technical development", "Manufacturing technology development"], "industries": ["Automotive"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Design, develop, and manufacture integrated electrical distribution systems in-house", "Advanced product and manufacturing technology for electrified vehicles", "Systems integration and modularization expertise", "Global technical development and manufacturing footprint across North America", "Focus on developing people to continuously improve manufacturing capability"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1987 -> db", "Core business since 1987 -> /", "Headquarters Farmington Hills, MI -> /", "President Kazuyoshi Nakai -> /about-us", "Mission: global leader delivering innovative electrical distribution systems -> /about-us", "Vision principles: systems integration, modularization, global marketing, advanced technology, developing people -> /about-us", "Product categories: wiring harnesses, electronics, components, electric wire, electrified vehicle products, advanced product development -> /, /about-us", "Industries: automotive wiring harness and electronics markets, automotive industry -> /, /about-us", "Sumitomo 400-year heritage referenced -> /about-us", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "design, develop, and manufacture products the automotive industry wants", "founded_year": "1987", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/sumitomo-electric-wiring-systems/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sumitomo-electric-wiring-systems' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sumner Woodworker Store operates in Sumner, Washington, in a building with roots dating back to 1889. The business has been family-owned since 1996, when John and Joan Schmit — John a former Boeing executive who restored classic wooden boats — decided to open a woodworking store in a property they were renovating. The Schmit family''s personal passion for woodcraft shaped the store''s founding mission.

The store runs a nearly 10,000-square-foot retail facility stocked with woodworking tools, supplies, and a wide selection of exotic and premium woods. It carries brands such as SuperMax drum sanders, SawStop professional cabinet saws, Robert Sorby woodturning tools, and Colwood wood-burning tools. Every tool sold is inspected, assembled, and tested before it leaves the store. The inventory includes nearly 100 species of wood, plus turning blocks, carving blocks, and pen-making materials. The staff is composed entirely of experienced woodworkers who provide hands-on product guidance.

The store serves hobbyist and professional woodworkers, woodcarvers, and some metalworkers. Its customer base ranges from DIY enthusiasts and small-shop professionals to woodturners seeking specialized tools and materials. It positions itself as a one-stop shop for woodworking and wood carving in Washington state.

The Schmit family started the business to offer a knowledgeable, non-commercialized alternative to big-box retailers. They differentiate by ensuring tools are ready to run out the door, maintaining deep product expertise, and preserving a historical store environment that reflects the community''s woodworking heritage.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Retail sales of woodworking tools and supplies", "Exotic and premium wood supply and selection", "Tool assembly, inspection, and testing", "Product knowledge and customer assistance", "Woodturning and carving tool specialization"], "industries": ["Woodworking", "Woodcarving", "Metalworking"], "materials": ["Exotic woods", "Premium woods", "Turning blocks", "Carving blocks", "Pen making materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned since 1996 with founders John and Joan Schmit", "Every tool inspected, assembled, and tested before sale", "Nearly 10,000 sq. ft. of retail space dedicated to woodworking", "One of Washington''s largest suppliers of exotic and premium woods", "Staff composed entirely of experienced woodworkers"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1889 -> db", "Family-owned since 1996 -> /", "Founders John and Joan Schmit -> /about", "John Schmit former Boeing executive, restored wooden boats -> /about", "Joan Schmit idea to open store in renovated building -> /about", "Nearly 10,000 sq. ft. retail space -> /", "Stock nearly 100 species of exotic/premium woods -> /", "Carry SuperMax drum sanders, SawStop cabinet saws, Robert Sorby tools, Colwood wood-burning tools -> /", "Every tool inspected, assembled, tested before sale -> /about", "Staff are all woodworkers with years of experience -> /about", "Serve hobbyists, professionals, woodcarvers, some metalworkers -> /, /about", "One of largest specialized woodworking stores in Washington -> /about", "Historical building and community history -> /about"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Nearly 10,000 square feet of retail space dedicated to Woodworking.", "founded_year": "1889", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sumner-woodworker-store' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sun Comm Technologies, Inc. was founded in 1993 in Santa Fe, New Mexico, and has since provided television programming and high-speed internet services to residential and commercial customers across New Mexico, West Texas, eastern Arizona, and southern Colorado.

The company acts as an authorized retailer and installer for major satellite and internet brands including DISH, DIRECTV, Spectrum, CenturyLink, HughesNet, and Viasat. It designs and installs integrated cable systems for hospitality, healthcare, and institutional clients, deploying 10 to 75 receivers per property. Services span satellite TV installation, broadband provisioning, and in-room entertainment casting solutions for hotels.

Sun Comm serves a diverse client base: hotels and motels, hospitals and assisted-living facilities, correctional institutions, military bases, state and federal government offices, college dormitories, and bars and restaurants. Residential customers in Albuquerque, Santa Fe, Las Cruces, and El Paso also make up a significant portion of its business.

