UPDATE companies SET description='Sun Medical Equipment & Supplies was founded in 1979 in Troy, Michigan, as a locally owned and operated business serving the home health needs of patients across Oakland, Macomb, and Wayne Counties. The company began with a focus on providing durable medical equipment and in-home care services that allow customers to remain comfortable at home.

The company operates a retail store in Troy and an online catalog, supplying home medical equipment from brands such as Philips, LIFEPAK, and AirMini. Its product range includes CPAP machines, AEDs, cold therapy systems, mobility aids, hospital beds, oxygen and respiratory equipment, bath safety items, compression garments, orthotic braces, wound care supplies, and power scooters. Sun Medical also provides in-home care staffed by nurses, home health aides, and caregivers, overseen by a registered nurse. The staff offers expertise in mobility equipment fitting, orthotic and compression garment fitting, Medicare billing, and home modification installation.

Sun Medical serves individual patients, union members (who receive exclusive discounts), and healthcare providers such as Corewell Health. The company works with professional organizations including the National Homecare & Hospice Association, the Michigan Homecare & Hospice Association, the Michigan Spinal Cord Injury Association, and the Case Management Society of America.

The company emphasizes its accreditation by the Community Health Accreditation Partner, Inc., and its commitment to staying at the forefront of industry changes to deliver quality service. It highlights 5-star customer ratings and a mission to provide everything from A to Z for comfort, independence, safety, and security at home.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["In-home nursing care", "Home health aide services", "Caregiver services", "Medical equipment sales and rental", "Mobility equipment fitting", "Orthotic and compression garment fitting", "Medicare billing assistance", "Home modification installation", "AED supply for workplaces", "Bath safety equipment installation", "Oxygen and respiratory equipment setup", "Wound care supply management"], "industries": ["Home healthcare", "Durable medical equipment", "Home medical equipment supply"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["AirMini Travel Portable CPAP Machine", "CryoCube Cold Therapy System", "LIFEPAK CR2 AED", "Philips HeartStart FRx AED"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Accredited by Community Health Accreditation Partner, Inc.", "In-home care program led by a registered nurse", "Exclusive discounts for union members", "Locally owned and operated since 1979", "Staff expertise in mobility equipment, orthotic/compression fitting, and Medicare billing"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 -> db", "Headquarters Troy, Michigan -> db", "Locally owned and operated -> /", "Serves Oakland, Macomb, Wayne Counties -> /", "Accredited by Community Health Accreditation Partner, Inc. -> /about-us", "In-home care program led by a Registered Nurse -> /services", "Union member discounts -> /", "Staff expertise in mobility equipment, orthotic and compression garment fitting, Medicare billing -> /about-us", "Product lines: AirMini Travel Portable CPAP Machine, CryoCube Cold Therapy System, LIFEPAK CR2 AED, Philips HeartStart FRx AED -> /", "Professional associations: Corewell Health, National Homecare & Hospice Association, Michigan Homecare & Hospice Association, Michigan Spinal Cord Injury Association, Case Management Society of America -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Sun Medical Equipment & Supplies is a locally owned and operated company focused on serving the home health needs of patients in Oakland, Macomb, and Wayne Counties. Since 1979, we have been providing home medical equipment and home care services...", "founded_year": "1979", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sun-medical-equipment-company-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sun Solar LLC was founded in 2012 by Caleb Arthur in Houston, Missouri, before moving its headquarters to Springfield, Missouri. Arthur, a former law enforcement officer, turned to solar after a career-ending injury, initially installing a ground-mount system on his own property and then selling and installing systems door-to-door. The company now serves Missouri, Kansas, and Illinois from its Springfield base.

The company provides turnkey solar installation services for residential and commercial customers, handling design, permitting, coordination, installation, electrification, and ongoing service. Its offerings include rooftop and ground-mount solar arrays, Tesla Solar Roof installations (the first in Missouri), and Tesla Powerwall battery backup systems. A dedicated Smart Energy Solutions division adds energy-efficiency upgrades such as LED lighting, attic sealing, and insulation. Financing options span loans, cash purchases, and power purchase agreements.

Sun Solar works primarily with homeowners and businesses across the three-state region. Residential clients include individual households seeking energy independence, while commercial customers range from small businesses to larger facilities such as the Denton Embassy Suites. The company also partners with Everbright Exteriors for roofing services.

Arthur’s “reduce before you produce” philosophy drives the firm’s focus on energy efficiency alongside solar generation, aiming to lower both utility bills and environmental impact.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar panel installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Tesla Solar Roof installation", "Battery backup installation (Tesla Powerwall)", "Solar financing (loan, cash, power purchase agreement)", "Energy efficiency upgrades (LED lighting, attic sealing, insulation)", "System design and permitting", "System monitoring and service"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2012 by Caleb Arthur -> /about", "Headquartered in Springfield, Missouri -> /about", "Serves Missouri, Kansas, Illinois -> /about", "Offers residential and commercial solar installation -> /services", "Installs Tesla Solar Roof and Powerwall -> /services", "Provides energy efficiency upgrades via Smart Energy Solutions -> /services", "Financing options: loan, cash, PPA -> /services", "13,000+ customers -> /", "First Tesla Solar Roof in Missouri -> /services", "Reduce before you produce philosophy -> /about", "Company name and website -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We design, permit, coordinate, install, electrify, and service your system.", "founded_year": "2012", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sun-solar-illinois' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SunCommon is headquartered in Waterbury, Vermont, and has been operating in New York since 2002 and in Vermont since 2012. The company was founded in 2002 and is structured as a certified B Corporation and a benefit corporation, reflecting a mission-driven ownership model that balances profit with social and environmental impact.

The company provides full-service solar and energy storage installation for residential, commercial, agricultural, non-profit, and municipal customers. Its services cover roof-mounted and ground-mounted solar arrays, battery backup systems (including Tesla Powerwall), electric vehicle charger installation, and community solar array development. SunCommon manages the entire project lifecycle — planning, financing, permitting, design, engineering, and construction — and reports having served over 10,000 customers across its two-state territory.

SunCommon’s customer base spans homeowners, businesses, farms, non-profits, and municipalities in Vermont and New York. Specific examples include residential rooftop and ground-mount systems, commercial solar projects that qualify for additional incentives, farm installations described as a “no-brainer” by the company, and community solar arrays that allow multiple utility customers to share the output of a single one-acre array through group net metering.

The company says its distinguishing features are its status as the most tenured local solar provider in its regions, its certification as a B Corporation and benefit corporation, and its mission to accelerate the transition to solar power because “ensuring a habitable planet is the most important work of our lifetimes.” It also notes being named the reader’s choice for solar and batteries since 2016.', certifications=ARRAY['Certified B Corporation','Benefit Corporation']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar photovoltaic system design and installation (roof and ground mount)", "Battery energy storage system installation (Tesla Powerwall)", "Electric vehicle charger installation", "Community solar array development and management", "Project planning and financing", "Permitting and regulatory compliance", "Electrical engineering and system design", "Construction and commissioning", "Virtual and in-person site assessment"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Agricultural", "Non-profit", "Municipal", "Community solar", "Renewable energy"], "materials": ["Solar photovoltaic modules", "Lithium-ion battery storage systems (Tesla Powerwall)", "Electric vehicle charging equipment"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Certified B Corporation and benefit corporation structure", "Most tenured local solar company in Vermont and New York", "Full-service project management from planning through construction", "Community solar array development expertise", "Over 10,000 customers served since 2002"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Waterbury, Vermont -> db", "Founded in 2002 (New York) -> db", "Operating in Vermont since 2012 -> /", "Certified B Corporation -> /", "Benefit Corporation -> /", "Mission-driven company -> /", "Over 10,000 customers served -> /", "Services: roof/ground solar, battery storage, EV chargers, community solar -> /", "Full lifecycle: planning, financing, permitting, design, engineering, construction -> /", "Customer types: homes, businesses, farms, non-profits, municipalities -> /", "Community solar arrays (one-acre, group net metering) -> /about", "Reader''s choice for solar and batteries since 2016 -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "From planning and financing, through permitting, design, engineering, and construction, our team is there to make your experience smooth and hassle free.", "founded_year": "2002", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='suncommon' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sunbelt Packaging LLC began in 1980 in York, South Carolina, as a supplier of specialty products for niche applications in the textile industry. The company expanded into flexible packaging materials to leverage its service reputation and grew through acquisitions into a global provider. Today it operates as part of BradyPLUS Company, a larger platform offering tailored solutions for janitorial/sanitation, foodservice, and industrial packaging markets.

The firm supplies a range of flexible packaging materials including flexible intermediate bulk containers (FIBC), stretch films, shrink wrap, and strapping. It also sells and supports automated packaging equipment such as stretch wrappers, automatic strapping machines, palletizing robots with payloads from 6 kg to 1,200 kg, and continuous-motion wraparound case packers. Sunbelt services customers across all 50 U.S. states, Canada, Mexico, South America, and Singapore.

