UPDATE companies SET description='The company negotiated the state’s first net metering agreement in 1996 and helped shape North Carolina’s interconnection policy through Senate Bill 3 in 1998. In 2007 it relocated to Weaverville, where it built a 4,100-square-foot shop and supply warehouse in 2014.

The firm designs, installs, and services renewable energy systems including grid-tied and off-grid solar photovoltaics, battery storage, radiant floor heating, solar hot water, micro hydro, and wind power. It also manufactures the VersaCor, a standardized hydronic heating system introduced in 2002. Sundance serves residential and commercial clients, with a portfolio exceeding 2,000 installations by 2018. Its service department maintains systems originally installed by other contractors and offers annual maintenance agreements.

Customers span homeowners, businesses, institutions, and government agencies. Notable projects include a 600 kW array for Sierra Nevada Brewing’s Mills River facility, solar hot water at Camp Lejeune and Cherry Point, photovoltaic and solar thermal installations at Catawba College, and systems for the Catholic Diocese of Charlotte. The company has provided mobile solar power for the Indigo Girls’ Earth Day concert and the Standing Rock protests, and partnered with Duke Energy on a statewide rebate program.

Sundance differentiates itself through a five-step design process led by Renewable Energy Consultants who avoid high-pressure sales, a service team that works on any brand of equipment, and membership in the Amicus Solar Cooperative for collective buying power. Its early policy work established net metering and renewable energy credit markets in North Carolina, positioning the company as a long-standing advocate for clean energy adoption in the Carolinas.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar photovoltaic system design and installation", "Battery storage system design and installation", "Radiant floor heating system design and installation", "Solar hot water system design and installation", "System maintenance and repair", "Annual maintenance agreements", "VersaCor hydronic heating system manufacturing", "Renewable energy consulting", "Project management"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Military", "Education", "Hospitality", "Faith-based", "Brewing", "Non-profit", "Utility"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Mobile Solar Generator", "VersaCor hydronic heating system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Five-step design process led by non-commissioned Renewable Energy Consultants", "Service team maintains systems installed by any contractor", "Member of Amicus Solar Cooperative for collective component purchasing", "Pioneered North Carolina\u2019s first net metering agreement (1996) and interconnection policy (1998)", "Manufactures the VersaCor standardized hydronic heating system"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1995 -> db", "Headquarters in Weaverville, NC -> db", "Incorporated May 1995 to expand founders'' environmental work -> / timeline 1995", "First net metering agreement in NC 1996 -> / timeline 1996", "Helped pass SB3 interconnection policy 1998 -> / timeline 1998", "Relocated to Weaverville 2007 -> / timeline 2007", "Built 4,100 sq ft warehouse 2014 -> / timeline 2014", "Manufactures VersaCor hydronic heating system (2002) -> / timeline 2002", "Over 2,000 customers by 2018 -> / timeline 2018", "Service team works on other companies'' installations -> / description", "Five-step design process -> /services", "Renewable Energy Consultants not high-pressure sales -> /services", "Amicus Solar Cooperative member 2017 -> / timeline 2017", "600 kW system for Sierra Nevada Brewing 2014 -> / timeline 2014", "Solar hot water at Camp Lejeune and Cherry Point 2012 -> / timeline 2012", "PV and solar thermal at Catawba College 2014 -> / timeline 2014", "Systems for Catholic Diocese of Charlotte 2019 -> / timeline 2019", "Mobile solar generator for Indigo Girls concert 2000 -> / timeline 2000", "Mobile solar trailer for Standing Rock protests 2016 -> / timeline 2016", "Partnered with Duke Energy on rebate program 2017 -> / timeline 2017", "Offers annual maintenance agreements -> /services", "Service areas: North Carolina and South Carolina -> /services", "Battery storage, radiant floor heating, solar hot water listed as services -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "The VersaCor is the first product to be manufactured and distributed by Sundance Power Systems, Inc.", "founded_year": "1995", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sundance-power-systems-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sunergy Renewable Systems, LLC operates from Peosta, Iowa, where it was founded in 2017. The limited‑liability company was established to provide solar energy solutions across the Dubuque region, drawing on a team of contractors who collectively bring more than two decades of field experience.

The firm designs, installs, and services photovoltaic systems for residential, commercial, and agricultural customers. Its service lineup includes rooftop and ground‑mount solar panel installation, battery storage integration, system inspections, and ongoing repair and maintenance. Projects range from single‑home arrays to large‑scale installations for office buildings and senior‑living communities in the Peosta and Dubuque areas.

Customers span homeowners seeking lower utility bills, farms aiming to reduce reliance on conventional power, and businesses looking to cut operating costs while demonstrating sustainability commitments. The company holds Iowa Solar Contractor License C132504 and offers free consultations with upfront cost estimates for every project.

