ompany_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Whether you need solar panel installation, maintenance, or inspection, our trusted solar contractors are here to guide you every step of the way.", "founded_year": "2017", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sunergy-renewable-systems' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sunforce Solar, based in Las Cruces, New Mexico, was founded in 2020 by Obed Dominguez. The company began as a local startup with a vision to change how people think about energy, growing into a regional provider of solar installation services across multiple states.

The company designs, installs, and maintains complete clean-energy systems for residential and commercial customers. Services include rooftop and ground-mount solar panel installation, home battery backup systems, Level 2 EV charger installation, solar panel maintenance, and re-roofing to prepare structures for solar. Sunforce handles permitting, interconnection applications, and final inspection across its service territory, which spans New Mexico, Texas, Colorado, Arkansas, and Pennsylvania. The company emphasizes a $0-down financing model that allows homeowners to replace utility payments with system ownership.

Sunforce serves homeowners and businesses seeking to reduce electricity costs and adopt renewable energy. Its residential clients include property owners in Las Cruces, El Paso, Colorado Springs, Springdale, and Philadelphia. Commercial projects are also undertaken, though specific industrial sectors are not detailed. The company works with customers regardless of whether they originally purchased their system from another provider, offering maintenance and system additions.

Founder Obed Dominguez states the company was started to make solar easy and accessible, with a mission to under-promise and over-deliver. Sunforce differentiates itself by sizing systems around actual usage history rather than generic estimates, confirming utility export credits, and providing transparent information about incentives, including the expiration of the federal residential solar tax credit at the end of 2025.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar panel installation (roof and ground-mount)", "Home battery backup installation", "EV charger installation (Level 2)", "Solar panel maintenance (cleaning, inverter diagnostics, monitoring checks, repairs)", "Re-roofing for solar readiness", "System additions (expanding existing arrays)", "Permitting and interconnection management", "Energy usage analysis and system sizing"], "industries": ["Residential solar installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Renewable energy services", "Energy storage systems", "Electric vehicle charging infrastructure"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Systems sized around actual usage history, not generic per-square-foot estimates", "Handles permitting, interconnection, and final inspection", "$0-down financing with system ownership", "Services systems installed by other companies", "Transparent incentive guidance including federal tax credit expiration"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2020 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Las Cruces, NM -> db", "Founder Obed Dominguez -> /about-us", "Services: solar panel installation, battery backup, EV charger, maintenance, re-roofing -> /services", "Service states: New Mexico, Texas, Colorado, Arkansas, Pennsylvania -> /services", "Licensed and insured -> /", "5.0 rating across 120+ Google reviews -> /", "$0-down financing -> /services", "Federal tax credit ended Dec 31, 2025 -> /services", "Mission to under-promise and over-deliver -> /about-us", "Systems sized around actual usage history -> /services", "Handles permitting and interconnection -> /services", "Services systems installed by other companies -> /services", "Ambassador referral program -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are a fully licensed and insured installation company, delivering Residential & Commercial Solar Services across the states we serve.", "founded_year": "2020", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/sunforcesolarco/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sunforce-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sunlight Electric is based in Idaho Falls, Idaho, and traces its roots to 2002 when founder Robert Nichols began performing residential and commercial electrical work. After more than two decades as a union journeyman electrician, often traveling out of state for contract jobs, Nichols identified a local gap in green‑energy solutions such as solar installations, energy management systems, and EV charging. He launched the business under the Sunlight Electric name in August 2021 to stay closer to his family and serve the surrounding communities of Rexburg, Blackfoot, Pocatello, and Ashton.

The company provides a full range of electrical services for both homes and businesses, including electrical repair and troubleshooting, solar panel installation, lighting retrofits, backup generator installation and service, energy management systems, and electric‑vehicle charger installation.

Customers include residential homeowners seeking lower utility bills and modern lighting, as well as commercial clients such as general contractors and facility managers who need to limit downtime and reduce production losses. Recent projects cited in reviews include a solar installation for a private residence, an LED retrofit for a commercial facility, and ongoing electrical service for a property management firm.

Nichols has said he started the company because he repeatedly heard from people who could not get an electrician to return their calls, and he enjoys tackling difficult troubleshooting jobs that others avoid. Sunlight Electric emphasizes transparent pricing — publishing its hourly rates online — timely communication, and a policy of not invoicing until the work meets its quality standard.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical repair and troubleshooting", "Solar panel installation", "Lighting retrofits", "Backup generator installation and service", "Energy management systems", "Electric vehicle charger installation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Transparent pricing with hourly rates published on the website", "Timely responses to all calls and inquiries", "No invoice unless work meets 100% quality confidence", "Locally owned small business serving neighboring communities"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2002 -> db", "Headquarters Idaho Falls, Idaho -> db", "Owner Robert Nichols -> / (reviews)", "Launched August 2021 -> /about-us", "Team of over a dozen electricians -> /about-us", "Services: electrical repair, solar installation, lighting retrofits, generators, EV chargers -> /", "Transparent pricing with hourly rates -> /", "100+ five-star reviews -> /about-us", "Serves Idaho Falls, Pocatello, Rexburg, Blackfoot, Ashton -> /about-us", "Core values: quality service, timely responses, transparent pricing -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Sunlight Electric provides a full range of both residential and commercial electrical services within the Idaho Falls and Pocatello areas.", "founded_year": "2002", "employee_count": "12+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::j