UPDATE companies SET description='THACO INDUSTRIES USA LLC is headquartered in Gardena, California, and operates as the U.S. subsidiary of THACO INDUSTRIES, a sub-holding of the Vietnamese conglomerate THACO. The parent corporation traces its roots to Vietnam’s mechanical engineering sector, though a specific founding year for the U.S. entity is not publicly disclosed.

The company designs, tests, validates, and manufactures automotive components, assemblies, and spare parts for domestic and international vehicle makers. Its capabilities span stamping, plastic injection molding (including a 3,200‑ton press), precision CNC machining, welding and structural fabrication, surface treatment, painting, and final assembly.

It also produces semi‑trailers (skeletal, flatbed, dump, cargo) for North American and Australian markets, commercial and household goods (treadmills, pallets, shopping carts, plastic tanks) shipped to the U.S., Canada, Japan, and Australia, and high‑tech products including industrial robots, AGVs, AMRs, and drones. A notable reference is Ford Motor Company’s Q1 certification awarded to its plastic component division.

