UPDATE companies SET description='Team Solar Inc was founded in 2016 by brothers Jonathan and James Neal in Portland, Maine, with a second office in Framingham, Massachusetts. The two industry experts started the company to educate and advise property owners on renewable energy options, positioning themselves as consultants rather than traditional sales-driven installers.

The firm provides end‑to‑end solar services for commercial, residential, and non‑profit clients. Its process moves from an initial consultation through engineering and construction to a monthly payment structure, and the company reports having delivered roughly 1,900 kilowatts of installed capacity across 141 customers. A lean staff handles design, permitting, and project management for each installation.

Commercial property owners, homeowners, and a range of non‑profit organizations make up the customer base. The non‑profit program, which installs systems at no upfront cost and shares utility revenue with the host, has served VFW posts, American Legion halls, religious buildings, Boys & Girls Clubs, YMCAs, municipalities, and low‑income housing developments in Maine and Massachusetts.

The founders say the business was built on an educational focus that avoids aggressive sales tactics, customizing every proposal to the client’s financial situation and energy goals. That approach, they claim, helps customers achieve energy independence while stabilizing long‑term operating costs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar consulting and energy cost analysis", "Commercial solar development and installation", "Residential solar design and installation", "Non\u2011profit solar program (zero upfront cost)", "Engineering, permitting, and construction management", "Ongoing performance monitoring and monthly payment administration"], "industries": ["Commercial real estate", "Residential", "Non-profit organizations"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Educational consulting model rather than sales-driven approach", "No aggressive sales tactics; customized solutions for each client", "Non\u2011profit solar installations at zero upfront cost with shared revenue", "Simple four\u2011step process: consultation, engineering, construction, monthly payments", "Lean, passionate team focused on renewable technology"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2016 by Jonathan and James Neal -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Portland, ME and Framingham, MA -> /about-us", "1,900 kW solar sold, 141 customers -> /", "Services: commercial, residential, non-profit solar -> /services", "Non-profit program includes VFW, American Legion, religious buildings, Boys & Girls Clubs, YMCA, municipalities, low-income housing -> /services", "Process: consultation, engineering, construction, get paid monthly -> /services", "Educational focus, no aggressive sales tactics -> /about-us", "Lean staff passionate about renewable tech -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We help our clients create consistent recurring cash flow from solar.", "founded_year":