UPDATE companies SET description='Tekmos, Inc. is a fabless semiconductor company headquartered in Austin, Texas. Founded in 1997 as a spin-off of Flextronics Semiconductor, the company began as a contract design center handling FPGA conversions and large FPGA-based systems for on-demand cable providers.

Today Tekmos designs and manufactures custom analog and mixed-signal integrated circuits, including ASICs, FPGAs, microprocessors, flash memories, and high-temperature chips. The company leverages SOI CMOS processes for operation up to 300°C and bulk silicon up to 200°C, and offers stacked die packaging that combines up to nine different chips in a single package. With over 900 completed designs, Tekmos serves hundreds of customers worldwide, delivering volumes from prototype to over 100,000 units annually for individual part numbers.

The company serves consumer electronics, aerospace, automotive, defense, industrial, medical, oil and gas, and telecommunications markets. Concrete examples include supplying replacement processors for grounded military aircraft, high-temperature ASICs for downhole drilling steering, chips for fitness wearables and oral medical devices, and 60,000 emergency units to restore telephone service in New Orleans after Hurricane Katrina. Tekmos also recreated obsolete telecom ASICs for Lucent switches after Agere end-of-lifed the original parts.

Tekmos positions itself as a bridge between standard components and finished products, emphasizing low development risk, low cost, and fast time to market. Its differentiators include full military lot qualification (MIL-STD-883 and MIL-PRF-38535 flows), ITAR registration, AS9100D certification, and the ability to reverse-engineer legacy parts into modern, manufacturable designs.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR Registered','AS9100D','MIL-STD-883','MIL-PRF-38535']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom analog and mixed-signal IC design", "ASIC design and manufacturing", "FPGA to ASIC conversion", "Legacy IC replacement and reverse engineering", "High-temperature IC design (SOI CMOS up to 300\u00b0C, bulk silicon up to 200\u00b0C)", "Stacked die packaging (up to 9 chips)", "Multi-chip module integration", "MIL-STD-883 screening and qualification", "MIL-PRF-38535 flows", "Obsolete part replication", "Consumer ASIC cost reduction (sub $0.50)", "Quick-turn prototype to production"], "industries": ["Consumer Electronics", "Aerospace", "Automotive", "Defense", "Industrial", "Medical", "Oil and Gas", "Telecommunications"], "materials": ["Silicon (SOI CMOS)", "Silicon (bulk)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1997 as spin-off of Flextronics Semiconductor -> /about", "Headquarters Austin, Texas -> /", "Fabless semiconductor company -> /about", "Over 900 completed designs -> /about", "AS9100D certified -> /about", "ITAR registered -> /", "MIL-STD-883 & MIL-PRF-38535 flows available -> /", "High temperature up to 300\u00b0C SOI CMOS -> /about", "Stacked die packaging up to 9 chips -> /about", "Industries: consumer, aerospace, automotive, defense, industrial, medical, oil and gas, telecom -> /, /about", "60K units rush order for Hurricane Katrina -> /about", "Military aircraft replacement parts -> /about", "Legacy part replacement via reverse engineering -> /about", "Sub $0.50 consumer ASIC pricing -> /about", "180nm technology, QFN packages, multi-site testing -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Tekmos makes integrated circuits and is an ITAR Registered Company", "founded_year": "1997", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tekmos' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Telan Corporation operates from an 18,000-square-foot facility in Hatfield, Pennsylvania. The company was founded in 2003 and is led by President and CEO Conrad J. Nelson, with Shawn Goodwin as Director of Operations & Purchasing and George Kohn as Plant Manager & Quality Assurance.

Telan specializes in contract electronics manufacturing, providing printed circuit board assembly services that span surface-mount, through-hole, and mixed-technology processes. The facility supports both lead-free and leaded soldering using reflow ovens, wave soldering, and fully automated selective soldering equipment, along with hand soldering for delicate requirements. Additional capabilities include conformal coating, automated optical inspection (Mirtec MV-3), functional testing, box-build assembly, and PCB sourcing for consignment or turnkey programs. The shop handles high-volume, low-mix production as well as small-quantity runs.

